; parity.exe compares the rasterizing rules with rasterio's on tessera-eval's
; Austria labels and GeoTessera's landmasks. It needs those files and
; rasterio's rasters, which live outside the repository, so no test runs it:
;   parity.exe project DIR   writes DIR/jord_*.npy, the labels in UTM 33N;
;   (rasterio, outside the repository, writes DIR/<tile>.* from them);
;   parity.exe compare DIR MASKS   prints the cells where the owners differ,
;     on the grids of the landmasks MASKS/<tile>.tiff, read by Nx_io.load_tiff;
;   parity.exe landmask FILE...    prints each landmask's grid, system, nodata
;     and land cells.

(executable
 (name parity)
 (libraries jord jord_geotiff jord_geojson nx nx.io jsont jsont.bytesrw))
